- * Replace every run of 4 or more digits, where single spaces or hyphens may split the digits, so a one-time code is
- * never stored. Codes that mix letters and digits, or have fewer than 4 digits, are left alone (documented residual).
+ * Remove zero-width characters, then replace every run of 4 or more Unicode decimal digits, where one separator
+ * character may sit between neighbouring digits, so a one-time code is never stored. Codes that mix letters and
+ * digits, have fewer than 4 digits or use a multi-character separator are left alone (documented residual).
  */
